{
  "_doc": [
    "Reference vectors of whole inputs holding an image or an audio, for the EmbeddingGemma 2 pipeline (generated by tools/export-recipes/embeddinggemma2/multimodal_reference.py).",
    "Upstream: SentenceTransformer of the pinned snapshot, f32 on the CPU; each case is one `encode` call of an upstream dict input (its keys in the parts' order; an audio as its f32 samples at 16 kHz), with the prompt name when the case has one.",
    "The tensors of multimodal-reference.safetensors: `image.<name>` U8 [height, width, 3] (row-major RGB8, what upstream's processor read), `audio.<name>` F32 [samples] (16 kHz mono, what upstream's processor read), `audio.<name>.features` F32 [L, 128] (the valid log-mel frames upstream's feature extractor made of them; its frames after them are zeros), `<case>.input_ids` I32 [T] (the ids the composite model received, `<bos>` and `<eos>` included, each image as `<|image>` + n x `<|image|>` + `<image|>`, each audio as `<|audio>` + m x `<|audio|>` + `<audio|>`), `<case>.embedding` F32 [768] (the normalised vector `encode` returned).",
    "`cases` hold images only; `audioCases` hold an audio (and an image in one of them).",
    "`idCases` pin the ids alone where a text meets an image (no vector): each is one user message of content parts in order, its ids caught as for the other cases.",
    "`composition` is Karume's graphs composed in torch f32 (the tower wrappers' soft tokens at the placeholder rows of the text wrapper) against upstream's vector.",
    "The images and waveforms are synthetic and neutral (tools/export-recipes/embeddinggemma2/images.py, waveforms.py); do not add others."
  ],
